37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings bring a gentle warning. It seems that projects based on comfort or appeal often slip by a year or more, and we have lost many weeks to the rain and frost.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"That's a bit worrying, Shizue! I found something interesting too. It looks like our general-purpose rooms are super crowded all year, while the specialist rooms are often just sitting empty!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings reveal a concerning disconnect. While some newer posts have capacity, our bench technicians are still burdened with several hours of manual checks and window-opening routines because our extraction equipment is insufficient.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings suggest a clear pattern: projects that provide shared accessibility are rated highest by users, while those benefiting only a single wing are viewed as disappointments. Additionally, hazardous materials in older blocks are causing significant delays.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are all discovering that our theoretical plans are rather optimistic. My findings show that mechanical costs are surging, while we've neglected to set aside reserves for replacing essential audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, it sounds as though your technicians are working very hard under difficult conditions. It would be so kind of us to find a way to ease their daily burdens and bring them some peace.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I totally agree with Shizue! It sounds so stressful for the technicians. We should definitely look for a plan that helps them out! Also, @Mizuki, your findings match mine—shared spaces are definitely the way to go!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George"",""Shizue"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, @Yumi, I appreciate your concern. It is not just about stress, but a systemic inefficiency. We cannot continue to rely on manual workarounds for essential equipment while our staff is stretched thin.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I agree. Systemic inefficiency is a risk to everyone. If we combine your need for operational relief with my finding that shared accessibility brings the most satisfaction, we can find a truly effective solution.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is fascinating how we are all describing the same tragedy from different angles. We are essentially planning for a fantasy world where costs are static and equipment lasts forever, while the reality of the market remains inconveniently ignored.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, your words have a touch of wit, but they remind us to be humble. If we choose a project that is too ambitious or relies on ""appeal,"" we risk the same delays I found, which only adds to the stress of everyone involved.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, you're so right! We have to be careful. I'm also worried that if we don't think about the timetable, the work might get in the way of classes. We should find a plan that's helpful but doesn't cause a big mess!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I agree that avoiding chaos is important. However, we must not let the fear of a ""mess"" prevent us from addressing the actual failures of our infrastructure. A plan that ignores the technicians' burden is not a sustainable plan.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand your position. However, we must also be mindful of the physical risks. My data shows that ground-floor work in older blocks often reveals hazardous materials, which could lead to the very chaos @Yumi fears.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Your collective caution is quite refreshing. It seems we are in agreement that the ideal candidate must be a pragmatic one: low risk, high utility, and, crucially, financially grounded in current market rates rather than hopeful estimates.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Benjamin. Let us seek a path that is gentle on our budget and our people. A plan that is realistic and avoids the pitfalls of ""appeal"" will bring us all a sense of peace.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm with you all! Let's find a plan that's really useful for everyone, helps the technicians, and doesn't cause any big delays. I'm sure we can find a perfect choice that makes everyone happy!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,George,,"I agree. While I appreciate the desire for harmony, we must be firm about the operational requirements. I will be looking for a candidate that specifically reduces the manual burden on our staff.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. We should prioritize a candidate that balances operational relief with shared utility, while strictly avoiding the older blocks to ensure we don't encounter hazardous materials and unpredictable delays. I am ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It appears we have successfully mapped the minefield of our current institutional failings. I shall await the candidates with a measured hope that at least one of them possesses the grace to be both useful and affordable.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
57,2,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
