63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at our options, Plan D seems the most harmonious. It addresses the burdens @George mentioned and, as a necessary upgrade, it is far more likely to stay on schedule than a project based on appeal.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with Shizue! Plan D sounds wonderful because it helps the technicians and it's for shared labs, which matches what @Mizuki and I found about shared spaces being the most helpful for everyone!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,George,,Plan D is the only logical choice. It directly addresses the insufficient extraction equipment and eliminates the manual routines that have burdened our technicians for far too long. It is a necessary operational fix.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Plan D provides the shared utility that users value most and solves the operational failures George identified. Crucially, it avoids the ground-floor risks of Plan C, ensuring we don't face hazardous material delays.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan D is indeed the most pragmatic. While Plan A's surfacing costs are stable, it offers little utility. Plan B would be a financial fantasy given our lack of AV renewal reserves. Plan D is a necessary investment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing when we all find such unity in our purpose. By choosing Plan D, we are not only improving our facilities but also showing kindness to the people who keep them running.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! It feels great to pick something that helps the technicians and gives students better shared spaces. I just hope we can schedule it carefully so it doesn't disrupt the classes!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, scheduling is a matter of management, but the need for this upgrade is a matter of necessity. We cannot prioritize a tidy timetable over the basic operational health of our laboratories and the well-being of our staff.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I agree that necessity must come first. Since Plan D is an essential infrastructure upgrade rather than a luxury, it is the most stable choice. It satisfies our requirements for utility, staff relief, and risk mitigation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is a refreshing change of pace to reach a consensus with such efficiency. We have successfully navigated the labyrinth of systemic risks to find a truly viable path. I find the logic inescapable; to choose otherwise would be to invite the very frictions we have identified.,"{""words"":47,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel a great sense of peace knowing we have found a solution that cares for everyone. Let us move forward with a heart full of confidence in this choice. I am ready to cast my vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm ready too! It's just so wonderful that we found a plan that helps the technicians and makes the labs better for everyone. I'm super happy to vote for Plan D!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,George,,I concur. Plan D is the only proposal that treats the operational strain on our staff as a priority rather than an afterthought. I am ready to cast my vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. Plan D is the only candidate that aligns with all our findings: it provides shared utility, relieves the operational burden on staff, and avoids the hazardous risks of the older blocks. I vote for Plan D.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I find myself in complete agreement. Plan D is the only option that balances operational necessity with financial realism, avoiding the AV void of Plan B and the hazardous pitfalls of Plan C. I vote for Plan D.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It has been a true privilege to deliberate with you all. In our unity, we have found a path that honors both the science and the scientists. I cast my final vote for Plan D.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,This was such a great experience! I'm so glad we could all work together to find a plan that helps the technicians and the students. I cast my final vote for Plan D!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,George,,I am satisfied that we have reached a decision based on necessity and operational reality. It is a relief to finally address the burdens placed on our staff. I cast my final vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I am satisfied that we have reached a consensus that is both logical and compassionate. By prioritizing shared utility and operational health, we have made the most responsible choice for the campus. I cast my final vote for Plan D.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It has been a most pleasant collaboration. We have managed to align our institutional ambitions with the stubborn realities of the market and the archives. I cast my final vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
